  "hints": [
    "The ranks only depend on the relative order of the values. Which collection of values do you need in sorted order?",
    "Take the distinct values, sort them, and map each value to its index + 1.",
    "A dictionary value -> rank gives O(1) lookups; alternatively binary search each value in the sorted distinct array. Both are O(n log n) overall."
  ],
  "editorial": "Sort the distinct values; the rank of `v` is its index in that list plus one. Looking ranks up through a hash map is expected `O(1)` each and a binary search is `O(log n)`; either way the cost is dominated by the `O(n log n)` sort.\n\nThis *coordinate compression* turns huge value ranges (`10^9`) into small dense indices `1..n`, which can then index arrays, Fenwick trees or bitsets.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n log n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\n# coordinate compression\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\n# your code here\n",
    "javascript": "// coordinate compression\n// readLine() returns the next input line (or null).\n// your code here\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    // coordinate compression\n    return 0;\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        // coordinate compression\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn = int(data[0])\na = list(map(int, data[1:1+n]))\nrank = {v: i + 1 for i, v in enumerate(sorted(set(a)))}\nprint(' '.join(str(rank[x]) for x in a))\n",
    "javascript": "const n = parseInt(readLine());\nconst a = readLine().trim().split(/\\s+/).map(Number);\nconst uniq = Array.from(new Set(a)).sort((x, y) => x - y);\nconst rank = new Map();\nuniq.forEach((v, i) => rank.set(v, i + 1));\nconsole.log(a.map((x) => rank.get(x)).join(' '));\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StreamTokenizer in = new StreamTokenizer(new BufferedInputStream(System.in));\n        in.nextToken();\n        int n = (int) in.nval;\n        long[] a = new long[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { in.nextToken(); a[i] = (long) in.nval; }\n        long[] s = a.clone();\n        Arrays.sort(s);\n        int m = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) if (i == 0 || s[i] != s[i - 1]) s[m++] = s[i];\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (i > 0) sb.append(' ');\n            sb.append(Arrays.binarySearch(s, 0, m, a[i]) + 1);\n        }\n        System.out.println(sb);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (auto &x : a) cin >> x;\n    vector<long long> s = a;\n    sort(s.begin(), s.end());\n    s.erase(unique(s.begin(), s.end()), s.end());\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        int r = lower_bound(s.begin(), s.end(), a[i]) - s.begin() + 1;\n        cout << r << (i + 1 < n ? ' ' : '\\n');\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n"
